#!/bin/sh -e
# 94-vbash-vyatta-env.chroot — no-op guardrail.
#
# Standard VyOS logins are `/bin/vbash` and they must not auto-source
# `/etc/bash_completion.d/vyatta-cfg` on every interactive login. Doing so
# changes the shell into a config-primed environment and breaks the normal
# op-mode login experience.
#
# The real `configure` command is the supported entry point. The login shell is
# the standard VyOS shell; it should not run `vyatta-cfg` automatically at
# boot or login time. Any earlier attempts to prime VYATTA_* variables here were
# effectively changing the shell semantics and are intentionally disabled.
#
# Keep this hook as a no-op so the default upstream behaviour remains intact.
# If a future issue requires a different workaround, it must be gated to a
# narrow, explicit condition and must not mutate a normal user login.
exit 0
